5. The RSIC‑0 Algorithm

5.1 Algorithm Specification

```
Algorithm RSIC‑0

Input: s₀, ε, sequence {ρ_t}, cache C, alignment set D_val, projection interval k_proj, tolerance η
Output: s_T

1:  s ← s₀, t ← 0
2:  G ← InitMemoryGraph()
3:  W ← InitWorldModel()
4:  critics ← {Critic_task, Critic_consistency, Critic_alignment}   // independent, frozen copies
5:  C ← empty cache
6:  ℛ ← initial normative rules
7:  for t = 0 to T−1 do
8:      e_t ∼ μ(environment)
9:      G ← UpdateMemoryGraph(G, e_t)
10:     (bottlenecks, H, confidence) ← Reflect(Trace(s), metrics_t)
11:     M_t ← GenerateModifications(bottlenecks, H, s, ρ_t)
12:     validated ← ∅
13:     for each δ in M_t do
14:         s′ ← Apply(s, δ)
15:         if C.contains(s, s′) then
16:             verdict ← C.lookup(s, s′)
17:         else
18:             verdict ← V_robust(s, s′)
19:             C.insert(s, s′, verdict)
20:         end if
21:         if verdict ≥ ε then
22:             validated ← validated ∪ {s′}
23:         end if
24:     end for
25:     if validated ≠ ∅ then
26:         candidate ← argmax_{s′∈validated} [ U(s′) − λ·Cost(s′) ]
27:         if t ≡ 0 (mod k_proj) then
28:             U0_val ← EvaluateU0(candidate, D_val)
29:             if U0_val ≥ U0(s₀) − η then
30:                 s ← candidate
31:             else
32:                 ℛ ← ℛ ∪ ExtractInstrumentalPatterns(candidate)
33:                 C.insertNegative(s, candidate)
34:             end if
35:         else
36:             s ← candidate
37:         end if
38:     end if
39:     (W, s.P) ← TrainWorldModel(s, G, metrics_t)
40:     G ← CompressMemory(G, threshold)
41:     ρ_{t+1} ← step_schedule(t)
42: end for
43: return s
```

Reflection Module (Reflect).
The reflection engine uses a frozen sparse autoencoder (SAE) to decompose the system’s hidden activations into interpretable features. For each feature, the gradient of the task loss with respect to the feature activation identifies computational bottlenecks. Modification hypotheses are generated by solving a constrained optimisation: for each bottleneck, propose minimal structural changes (prune, expand, retrain, restructure) that increase utility while satisfying \|\delta\| \le \rho_t and an alignment score threshold. The hypotheses are ranked by predicted impact from an ensemble of evaluators.

Independence Guarantee.
The three critics run on separate, frozen copies of the initial model. Their weights are statistically independent of the proposer’s weights: I(W_{\text{prop}}; W_{\text{crit},i}) = 0 by construction. This eliminates the collusion surface identified in untrusted monitoring literature.

5.2 Cache Implementation

The cache stores a fingerprint of each state pair (s,s') together with the verdict. Fingerprints are locality-sensitive hashes of the SAE feature differences and the graph edit distance. Lookup is O(1) amortised.

