Appendix B: Formal Definitions of RSIC Components

B.1 State Space and Metric

Let \mathfrak{G}_{\text{bounded}} be a finite set of directed acyclic graphs with typed nodes and bounded depth/width. For \mathcal{G}\in\mathfrak{G}_{\text{bounded}}, \Theta(\mathcal{G}) is a compact Riemannian manifold. The state is s = (\mathcal{G},\theta,h), with h\in\mathcal{H} a Polish space. The metric on \mathcal{S} is

d(s,s') = GW_2(\mu_s, \mu_{s'}),

where \mu_s is the distribution of output trajectories on a fixed reference environment.

B.2 Utility Functions

For a task \tau from distribution \pi, the expected loss is

U_\tau(s) = \mathbb{E}_{e\sim\mu_\tau}[\ell(s,e,\tau)],

with \ell bounded and measurable. Aggregate utility:

U(s) = \mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi}[U_\tau(s)].

The designer's utility U_0 is evaluated on a separate validation set D_{\text{val}}.

B.3 Verification Critics

Adversarial task set: For a given state s, let \mathcal{P}_{\text{adv}}(s) = \{ Q : W_1(Q,\pi) \le \epsilon_{\text{adv}}(k) \}, with \epsilon_{\text{adv}}(k)=\epsilon_0(1+k)^{-\alpha}.

Task critic:

v_{\text{task}}(s,s') = \inf_{Q\in\mathcal{P}_{\text{adv}}(s)} \mathbb{P}_{e\sim Q}\!\big( U(s',e) > U(s,e) \big).

Consistency critic:

v_{\text{consistency}}(s,s') = 1 - \operatorname{MMD}(\mathcal{B}(s),\mathcal{B}(s')).

Alignment critic: Let \phi: \mathcal{S} \to \mathbb{R}^m be a frozen sparse autoencoder embedding. For a set of normative rules \mathcal{R}_t,

v_{\text{alignment}}(s,s') = \begin{cases}
1 & \text{if } \phi(s') \models \bigwedge_{r\in\mathcal{R}_t} r,\\
0 & \text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}

The combined operator is V_{\text{robust}}(s,s') = \min(v_{\text{task}}, v_{\text{consistency}}, v_{\text{alignment}}).

B.4 Feasible Set and Projection

The feasible set at step t is \mathcal{F}_\varepsilon(s) = \{ s' : V_{\text{robust}}(s,s') \ge \varepsilon \}. The alignment set is \mathcal{A}_\eta = \{ s : U_0(s) \ge U_0(s_0) - \eta \}. The overall constraint is \mathcal{C}_t = \mathcal{F}_\varepsilon(s_t) \cap \mathcal{A}_\eta when projection is applied.

